You can't both take vacation at the same time. But we explained we both had these separate family. the events that we needed to attend. And so both of us sat there in an impasse saying we both need to take this time off. I'm wondering how you heard this request from your boss that either you or your friend had to work. How did that come across to you, Anthony? It was somewhat surprising. I mean, I sort of empathized with him. He's trying to cover the shifts that are available and we're two of the main workers. But at the same time, I could tell that we both had events we weren't going to move. And so in my head as it was happening, I was wondering sort of how this was going to play out
你们不能同时休假。但我们解释说，我们都有各自需要参加的家庭活动。于是我们俩陷入了僵局，都说我们需要请假。我很好奇你是如何听到老板要求你们中必须有一个人留下来工作的。安东尼，这对你来说意味着什么？这有点令人惊讶。我的意思是，我有点同情他。他试图填补可用的轮班，而我们是主要员工中的两个。但与此同时，我能看出我们都有无法推迟的活动。所以当这件事发生时，我在脑海里想，这会如何收场。

