00:07:12.000 --> 00:08:08.000
flour. And so as an inbound planner, my number one job is to not run out of flour. So something happened in the course of this job that in some ways was very consequential for your life. Tell me what happened. Yeah, so I had gotten my degree in logistics. And so this was a logistics planning job. And I even grew up in a family business in the field of logistics. And so I thought myself a pretty good planner. But when it turned out I was actually in this role, I tried to run inventories at a very tight level. And it turns out if you run inventories tight and you run short on one, you have to get a replacement for it pretty quickly. But one ingredient that's hard to replace quickly is flour because it comes by a slow rail car.
面粉。所以作为一名入库计划员，我的首要工作就是不能让面粉断货。所以在这份工作中发生了一件事，在某种程度上对你的人生影响深远。告诉我发生了什么。是的，我获得了物流学位。所以这是一份物流计划工作。我甚至是在一个从事物流行业的家族企业中长大的。所以我认为自己是一个相当不错的计划员。但当我真正担任这个角色时，我试图将库存保持在非常紧凑的水平。事实证明，如果你库存紧凑，一旦短缺，就必须很快找到替代品。但有一种原料很难快速更换，那就是面粉，因为它是由缓慢的铁路货车运输的。

14
00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:40.000
And so while I was running inventories tight, there was a rail car delay. and the plant had to shut down because I ran it out of flour. Wait, the whole plant had to shut down? Yes, so we're talking tens of thousands of dollars in cost because of my inventory management practices. I mean, the main feeling that I had was embarrassment and shame over, you know, there were a lot of people counting on this plant for livelihood and a lot of people counting on it for their breakfast.
所以当我在紧凑运行库存时，发生了一次铁路货车延误。工厂不得不停工，因为我把面粉用完了。等等，整个工厂不得不停工？是的，因为我的库存管理做法，造成了数万美元的损失。我的意思是，我当时的主要感觉是尴尬和羞愧，你知道，有很多人指望这家工厂维持生计，也有很多人指望它提供早餐。

