accepted into grad school and we sort of planned to move and live there for a long time, ended up taking a transfer to Lodi, California, to another manufacturing plant. And then after that, another manufacturing plan. So it really really diverted the professional course of my career, as well as the personal course of our lives as well. So, Anthony, your experience at the lumberyard and at General Mills can show how a single moment, whether that's a mistake or a conversation, can get us out of the usual way we run our lives, which is most commonly on autopilot. I want to talk about how sometimes these moments that give us clarity can grow out of very small thoughts and feelings. You like to tell the story about a famous leader in the world of English soccer.
